craze's Responses API driver
============================

This package, and its Fantasy adapter in the package above it
(internal/harness/llm/responses_adapter.go), take their design from
Fantasy's OpenAI Responses language model:

    https://github.com/charmbracelet/fantasy
    charm.land/fantasy v0.43.2
    providers/openai/responses_language_model.go

-- the mapping of a conversation's messages to Responses input items
(toResponsesPrompt), of a stream's events to Fantasy stream parts (Stream),
and of a response's usage (responsesUsage). The code here is craze's own,
written against the standard library rather than the OpenAI SDK, and it
differs where the ChatGPT plan's route needs it to (plan 033 §3.9): the
system prompt always goes in instructions; reasoning effort and its summary
are sent for every model; max_output_tokens is never sent; tools go in one
namespace; encrypted reasoning is read from each item's end and replayed;
items are assembled from response.output_item.done; and success is
response.completed alone.

